      <h1 id="stage-11-reuse" class="group scroll-mt-20">Stage 11: Reuse<a href="#stage-11-reuse" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Store common steps, notes, and list items in two topics under <code>shared/</code>. Reuse those elements with <code>@conref</code>, <code>@conkeyref</code>, and <code>@conrefend</code>. Use conref push to insert a step at a target in another topic.</p>
      <p>Include the shared topics in the map as resources. DITA-OT processes their content without publishing separate pages for them.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 30 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 10 complete.</p>
      <p>For the core course, focus on pulling steps with <code>conref</code> and notes with <code>conkeyref</code>. The range and push examples are optional. See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/reference/choosing-reuse">Choose a reuse method</a> before adding shared content.</p>
      <p>Recorded output below is an example. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/run-the-gate">Check your work</a> to see the result for your own project.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-write-the-shared-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: Write the shared topics<a href="#step-1-write-the-shared-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><code>shared/common-steps.dita</code> A task whose steps exist to be referenced. Every reusable element has an <code>@id</code>.
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n<task id=\"common-steps\">\n  <title>Common steps</title>\n  <shortdesc>Reusable steps that other tasks pull in by conref. This task is a warehouse and is not published on its own.</shortdesc>\n  <taskbody>\n    <steps>\n      <step id=\"select-region\">\n        <cmd>Select the region of audio you want to work on.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>Click and drag in the waveform to select a region; the selection is highlighted.\n          To select the whole track, press <uicontrol>Ctrl+A</uicontrol> (Windows and Linux) or <uicontrol>Cmd+A</uicontrol> (macOS).</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n      <step id=\"save-project\">\n        <cmd>Save the project with <menucascade><uicontrol>File</uicontrol><uicontrol>Save Project</uicontrol><uicontrol>Save Project</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> saves the project as a single <keyword keyref=\"project-extension\"/> file in the folder you choose; the <wintitle>Save Project</wintitle> dialog suggests your Documents folder.</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n      <!-- Conref push: this step is inserted before the marked step in the recording task. -->\n      <step conaction=\"pushbefore\">\n        <cmd>Turn the playback volume down before you listen.</cmd>\n        <info>\n          <p>A recording can be much louder than you expect; start low and turn it up.</p>\n        </info>\n      </step>\n      <step conaction=\"mark\" conref=\"../topics/recording-your-first-track.dita#recording-your-first-track/play-back\">\n        <cmd/>\n      </step>\n    </steps>\n  </taskbody>\n</task>"} lang="xml" title="shared/common-steps.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><code>shared/common-notes.dita</code> A generic <code>&lt;topic&gt;</code> for notes and a list. <code>&lt;topic&gt;</code> is the base type, with <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> instead of <code>&lt;conbody&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;taskbody&gt;</code>; a shared topic of notes has no reason to be a concept or a task.
      <CodeBlock code={"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN\" \"topic.dtd\">\n\n<topic id=\"common-notes\">\n  <title>Common notes</title>\n  <shortdesc>Reusable notes, tips and lists that other topics pull in by conref. This topic is a warehouse and is not published on its own.</shortdesc>\n  <body>\n    <note id=\"backup-warning\" type=\"warning\">This effect changes the audio data.\n    Save the project first; you can undo with <uicontrol>Ctrl+Z</uicontrol> (Windows and Linux) or <uicontrol>Cmd+Z</uicontrol> (macOS).</note>\n    <note id=\"quiet-room-tip\" type=\"tip\">For best results, record in a quiet room and position the microphone 15 to 30 cm from your mouth.</note>\n    <p>Recommended starting settings for Noise Reduction:</p>\n    <ul id=\"noise-reduction-settings\">\n      <li id=\"nr-first\">Noise reduction: 12 dB</li>\n      <li>Sensitivity: 6</li>\n      <li id=\"nr-last\">Frequency smoothing: 3</li>\n    </ul>\n  </body>\n</topic>"} lang="xml" title="shared/common-notes.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the files</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Both <code>&lt;shortdesc&gt;</code>s say what the file is for: a reader who opens it in the editor, or an agent that finds it in a search, learns at once that it is a shared topic and is not published.</li>
      <li>The step <code>save-project</code> uses <code>&lt;keyword keyref="project-extension"/&gt;</code> for <code>.aup3</code>, the key defined in stage 10; a shared topic step should not hard-code product facts either.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;ul id="noise-reduction-settings"&gt;</code> has ids on its first and last items, <code>nr-first</code> and <code>nr-last</code>, so a topic can pull the three items as a range.</li>
      <li>The last two steps are the push. <code>&lt;step conaction="pushbefore"&gt;</code> is the content to insert; the <code>&lt;step conaction="mark" conref="…"&gt;</code> that follows names, by an ordinary conref, the step in the recording task to insert it before. The pushed step has content; the marker has an empty <code>&lt;cmd/&gt;</code> because a step must have one to validate.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-put-the-shared-topics-in-the-map" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Put the shared topics in the map<a href="#step-2-put-the-shared-topics-in-the-map" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n@@ -9,6 +9,9 @@\n \n   <mapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>\n   <keydef keys=\"start-here\" href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n+  <!-- Warehouses: pulled in by conref and conkeyref, never pages of their own. -->\n+  <keydef keys=\"common-notes\" href=\"shared/common-notes.dita\"/>\n+  <topicref href=\"shared/common-steps.dita\" processing-role=\"resource-only\"/>\n \n   <topichead navtitle=\"Getting started\">\n     <topicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\" collection-type=\"family\">"} lang="diff" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the two forms</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;keydef keys="common-notes" href="shared/common-notes.dita"/&gt;</code> gives the notes shared topic a key. A keydef is resource-only, so the topic is part of the map's key space and is processed, but is not a page.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;topicref href="shared/common-steps.dita" processing-role="resource-only"/&gt;</code> does the same by path. <code>@processing-role="resource-only"</code> is what a keydef sets by default: the topic is read, so its conref push can act, but it gets no entry in the table of contents and no output page.</li>
      <li>The shared topics need to be in the map. A conref by path would resolve without it, but a conkeyref needs the key, and a conref push acts only when DITA-OT processes the pushing topic as part of the publication.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-pull-the-content-into-the-tasks" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Pull the content into the tasks<a href="#step-3-pull-the-content-into-the-tasks" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/trimming-audio.dita</code> The save step becomes a reference to the shared topic.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n@@ -34,11 +34,8 @@\n           <p>If you hear a click at the join, select a few milliseconds around it and apply <menucascade><uicontrol>Effect</uicontrol><uicontrol>Fade In</uicontrol></menucascade> or <uicontrol>Fade Out</uicontrol>.</p>\n         </info>\n       </step>\n-      <step>\n-        <cmd>Save the project with <menucascade><uicontrol>File</uicontrol><uicontrol>Save Project</uicontrol><uicontrol>Save Project</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd>\n-        <info>\n-          <p><keyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> saves the project as a single <filepath>.aup3</filepath> file in the folder you choose; the <wintitle>Save Project</wintitle> dialog suggests your Documents folder.</p>\n-        </info>\n+      <step conref=\"../shared/common-steps.dita#common-steps/save-project\">\n+        <cmd/>\n       </step>\n     </steps>\n     <result>"} lang="diff" title="topics/trimming-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/recording-your-first-track.dita</code> The tip comes in by key, the save step by path, and the play-back step gets the <code>@id</code> the push targets.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n+++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@\n       <p>This task walks you through making your first audio recording.\n       You need a microphone connected to your computer.\n       If you are new to audio terms such as sample rate and clipping, read <xref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/> first.</p>\n-      <note type=\"tip\">For best results, record in a quiet room and position the microphone 15 to 30 cm from your mouth.</note>\n+      <note conkeyref=\"common-notes/quiet-room-tip\"/>\n     </context>\n     <steps>\n       <step>\n@@ -55,8 +55,11 @@\n       <step>\n         <cmd>Click <uicontrol>Stop</uicontrol> when you are finished.</cmd>\n       </step>\n-      <step>\n+      <step id=\"play-back\">\n         <cmd>Click <uicontrol>Play</uicontrol> to listen to your recording.</cmd>\n+      </step>\n+      <step conref=\"../shared/common-steps.dita#common-steps/save-project\">\n+        <cmd/>\n       </step>\n     </steps>\n     <result>"} lang="diff" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><code>topics/removing-background-noise.dita</code> The warning by key, the select step by path, and the settings as a range.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/removing-background-noise.dita\n+++ b/topics/removing-background-noise.dita\n@@ -8,8 +8,7 @@\n     <context>\n       <p>Background noise such as hum from electronics, hiss from a microphone or fan noise degrades a recording.\n       The Noise Reduction effect learns what the noise sounds like from a section that contains nothing else, then removes it everywhere.</p>\n-      <note type=\"warning\">This effect changes the audio data.\n-      Save the project first; you can undo with <uicontrol>Ctrl+Z</uicontrol> (Windows and Linux) or <uicontrol>Cmd+Z</uicontrol> (macOS).</note>\n+      <note conkeyref=\"common-notes/backup-warning\"/>\n     </context>\n     <steps>\n       <step>\n@@ -19,8 +18,8 @@\n           You need at least half a second of noise-only audio.</p>\n         </info>\n       </step>\n-      <step>\n-        <cmd>Select that section by clicking and dragging in the waveform.</cmd>\n+      <step conref=\"../shared/common-steps.dita#common-steps/select-region\">\n+        <cmd/>\n       </step>\n       <step>\n         <cmd>Choose <menucascade><uicontrol>Effect</uicontrol><uicontrol>Noise Removal and Repair</uicontrol><uicontrol>Noise Reduction</uicontrol></menucascade>, then click <uicontrol>Get Noise Profile</uicontrol>.</cmd>\n@@ -36,9 +35,7 @@\n         <info>\n           <p>Recommended starting settings:</p>\n           <ul>\n-            <li>Noise reduction: 12 dB</li>\n-            <li>Sensitivity: 6</li>\n-            <li>Frequency smoothing: 3</li>\n+            <li conref=\"../shared/common-notes.dita#common-notes/nr-first\" conrefend=\"../shared/common-notes.dita#common-notes/nr-last\"/>\n           </ul>\n           <note type=\"caution\">Too much noise reduction makes voices sound metallic or underwater.\n           Start moderate, increase gradually, and use <uicontrol>Preview</uicontrol> before applying.</note>"} lang="diff" title="topics/removing-background-noise.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the references</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>@conref="../shared/common-steps.dita#common-steps/save-project"</code> is the same <code>file#topic/element-id</code> form as an <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code>, relative to the referencing topic, hence <code>../shared/</code>. The whole element, <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;info&gt;</code> and all, comes from the target.</li>
      <li><code>@conkeyref="common-notes/backup-warning"</code> is <code>key/element-id</code>: the key from the map names the topic, so the path is not in the topic. Move the shared topic and only the keydef changes.</li>
      <li><code>@conrefend</code> on the <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> makes the reference a range: every element from the <code>@conref</code> target to the <code>@conrefend</code> target, in this case all three list items, replaces the one <code>&lt;li&gt;</code>. Both targets must be siblings of the same type.</li>
      <li><strong>The </strong><code>&lt;cmd/&gt;</code><strong> placeholder.</strong> A conref'd <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> still has to validate as a <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> before it is resolved, and the DTD says a step contains a <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code>. So the referencing step carries an empty <code>&lt;cmd/&gt;</code> that the conref replaces. The same rule applies to any element whose content model requires a child. A <code>&lt;note conkeyref="…"/&gt;</code> needs nothing, because a note may be empty.</li>
      <li>The referencing element and the target must be the same element type, and the target may not need anything the referencing context does not allow. A <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> into <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, a <code>&lt;note&gt;</code> into <code>&lt;context&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;li&gt;</code>s into a <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-update-the-readme-check-your-work-and-check-what-was-published" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: Update the README, check your work and check what was published<a href="#step-4-update-the-readme-check-your-work-and-check-what-was-published" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line and the layout</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 10: keys.\n+You are on stage 11: reuse.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check your work</strong> The format command covers <code>shared/</code> too.
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita shared/*.dita"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Then check the project. In the editor, choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> and read the result in the <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel. From the command line, run:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml check ."} lang="bash" />
      <p>Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean, with warnings\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:18] — nothing references it\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/audacity-guide/out/full\noutput   clean (full)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and the output of full holds together. 2 unused keys above: worth knowing, and not treated as failures."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p><code>start-here</code> and <code>digital-audio</code> are defined for a later stage: stage 18 uses them in a new topic.</p>
      <p>The health stage resolves every <code>@conref</code> and <code>@conkeyref</code> to an element that exists and checks that each <code>conaction="mark"</code> finds its target. Rename the play-back step's id, for example to <code>playback</code>, and check your work. The check stops at health and names the reference that no longer resolves. Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/shared/common-steps.dita:29  @conref=\"../topics/recording-your-first-track.dita#recording-your-first-track/play-back\" — element id 'play-back' not found in recording-your-first-track.dita\n  (run project-health for the full report)\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:18] — nothing references it\nNot ready: stopped at health — the project itself has faults, so nothing was built and no output was read."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel, or <code>dogsbay-xml project-health .</code>, reports a broken element id and, under <code>Conref pushes</code>, this line:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Conref pushes (1):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/shared/common-steps.dita:29  <step> push target id 'play-back' not found in recording-your-first-track.dita"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The diagnostic names the id that the push looks for, <code>play-back</code>, not the new id. Restore the id and check again.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Check the output</strong> The check builds the guide into <code>out/full/</code>. The folder has one page per topic in the table of contents and nothing for the shared topics:
      <CodeBlock code={"find out/full -name '*.html' | sort"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"out/full/index.html\nout/full/topics/exporting-audio.html\nout/full/topics/installing-audacity.html\nout/full/topics/preparing-to-record.html\nout/full/topics/recording-your-first-track.html\nout/full/topics/removing-background-noise.html\nout/full/topics/supported-audio-formats.html\nout/full/topics/trimming-audio.html\nout/full/topics/what-is-audacity.html\nout/full/topics/what-is-digital-audio.html"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The folder does not contain <code>common-steps.html</code> or <code>common-notes.html</code>. Open <code>recording-your-first-track.html</code>: the step "Turn the playback volume down before you listen" sits before "Click Play", pushed there from the shared topic, and the task's own file never mentions it.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test two errors. First, use a <code>@conkeyref</code> with an undefined key. Change <code>common-notes/backup-warning</code> in the noise task to <code>common-note/backup-warning</code> and check your work. The check stops at health. Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/removing-background-noise.dita:11  @conkeyref=\"common-note/backup-warning\" — key 'common-note' not defined\n  (run project-health for the full report)\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:18] — nothing references it\nNot ready: stopped at health — the project itself has faults, so nothing was built and no output was read."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel, or <code>dogsbay-xml project-health .</code>, gives the full report:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Root map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nUndefined keys (1):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/removing-background-noise.dita:11  key 'common-note' not defined\nUnused keys (2):\n  start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]\n  digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:18]\n\nSummary\n  Undefined keys                1\n  Unused keys                   2"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Because health fails, the check does not build. To see what DITA-OT makes of the same fault, build the deliverable directly:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml build . full"} lang="bash" />
      <p>The first lines of the example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"full (html5) → /home/you/audacity-guide/out/full: FAILED — 1 error(s)\n    file:/home/you/audacity-guide/topics/removing-background-noise.dita:11 The @conkeyref attribute value 'common-note/backup-warning' cannot be resolved because it does not contain a key or the key is not defined. Using the @conref attribute as fallback if it exists."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>DITA-OT resolves <code>@conkeyref</code> only through the root map's key space, and an undefined key produces build error <code>DOTJ046E</code>: the note would be missing from the page. The health check reports the same key before anything is built.</p>
      <p>Undo the key change. Next, remove the placeholder. Replace the trimming task's <code>&lt;step conref="…"&gt;&lt;cmd/&gt;&lt;/step&gt;</code> with a self-closing <code>&lt;step conref="…"/&gt;</code>, and check your work. The file is no longer valid, and the check names it. Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   NOT CLEAN\n  invalid: /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n  (run project-health for the full report)\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:18] — nothing references it\nNot ready: stopped at health — the project itself has faults, so nothing was built and no output was read."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel, or <code>dogsbay-xml project-health .</code>, gives the line, column, and message:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Invalid files (1 of 13):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/trimming-audio.dita:\n    37:77  error: The content of element type \"step\" is incomplete, it must match \"((note|hazardstatement)*,cmd,(choices|choicetable|info|itemgroup|stepxmp|substeps|tutorialinfo)*,stepresult?,steptroubleshooting?)\"."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Validation fails before anything is resolved.</p>
      <p>Undo the change and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code> before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>@conref="file#topic/id"</code> replaces an element with a copy of another; <code>@conkeyref="key/id"</code> does the same through the key space.</li>
      <li><code>@conrefend</code> turns a reference into a range of sibling elements.</li>
      <li>Conref push: <code>conaction="pushbefore"</code> (or <code>pushafter</code>, <code>pushreplace</code>) on the content, then <code>conaction="mark"</code> with a <code>@conref</code> to the target, from the shared topic's side.</li>
      <li>A referencing element must still validate, so a conref'd <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> keeps an empty <code>&lt;cmd/&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>Shared topics go in the map as a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> or with <code>@processing-role="resource-only"</code>, and are not published.</li>
      <li>An undefined key behind a <code>@conkeyref</code> is a DITA-OT error, <code>DOTJ046E</code>.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="next-lesson" class="group scroll-mt-20">Next lesson<a href="#next-lesson" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
